# UPSTREAM.sha256 — integrity record for the utf8proc fork
#
# 56 records, one `<hex>  <path>` line each, in sha256sum format. Check with:
#
#     sha256sum -c UPSTREAM.sha256
#
# sha256sum ignores every line starting with `#`, so this header travels with
# the record and costs nothing at check time.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THIS RECORD IS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# It pins the bytes this repository carries that this fork did not write: the
# whole native core, upstream's complete test suite, upstream's build and
# tooling files, upstream's licence text, and the Unicode conformance fixtures
# in `testdata/`. Any later edit to any of those 56 files makes the check fail
# loudly, which is the point: the compiled bytes, the replayed corpora and the
# licence text all have to stay the bytes this record names.
#
# It is NOT a signature, NOT a Git object id, and NOT a re-derivation from
# upstream commit 79cdd5ab40c79afa559f689ffc13b76812dee1ac. It is a hash of
# this working tree as measured on 2026-10-03. See UPSTREAM.md for what the
# tree-to-commit anchor rests on, and for the separate git-blob cross-check.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TWO ORIGINS IN ONE FILE, NAMED EXPLICITLY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 50 records are utf8proc upstream bytes at tag v2.12.0 = 79cdd5ab40c79afa559f689ffc13b76812dee1ac:
#
#     utf8proc.h  utf8proc.c  utf8proc_data.c   -- the compiled core, 3 files, 1 TU
#     LICENSE.md  README.upstream.md  NEWS.md  MANIFEST  lump.md  Doxyfile
#     Makefile  CMakeLists.txt  utils.cmake  libutf8proc.pc.in
#     libutf8proc.pc.cmakein  cmake/utf8proc-config.cmake.in
#     test/**     (19 files)  -- upstream's own C test suite, kept whole
#     bench/**    (6 files)   -- kept for provenance, never compiled; see NOTICE.md
#     data/**     (4 files)   -- upstream's Julia generator path, never compiled
#
# 6 records are Unicode, Inc. data files fetched by this fork from unicode.org
# on 2026-10-03 and stored byte for byte. They are NOT utf8proc upstream bytes,
# and no upstream .paths entry shipped them -- `data/Makefile`'s `clean:` target
# deletes them, which is exactly why this fork commits them:
#
#     testdata/NormalizationTest.txt       https://www.unicode.org/Public/18.0.0/ucd/NormalizationTest.txt
#     testdata/GraphemeBreakTest.txt      https://www.unicode.org/Public/18.0.0/ucd/auxiliary/GraphemeBreakTest.txt
#     testdata/DerivedCoreProperties.txt  https://www.unicode.org/Public/18.0.0/ucd/DerivedCoreProperties.txt
#     testdata/Unicode-License-V3.txt     https://www.unicode.org/license.txt
#
# and 2 are derived from one of those by upstream's own recorded extraction rule
# (`data/Makefile:53-57`), not hand-written:
#
#     testdata/Lowercase.txt   section of DerivedCoreProperties.txt
#     testdata/Uppercase.txt   section of DerivedCoreProperties.txt
#
# Both derived files terminate in a bare `# Total code points:` line with no
# count and no trailing newline. That is upstream's `print(match(...))` output
# verbatim. A parser must tolerate it; do not "fix" the files.
#
# The five data files are under the Unicode Terms of Use, NOT under utf8proc's
# MIT grants. Nothing in this record says otherwise, and no claim of "the whole
# tree is MIT" is made anywhere in this package. See NOTICE.md.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE, AND WHY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Four upstream files are excluded because this fork edits them in place, so
# they are no longer byte-identical to upstream and a digest here would be false
# within hours. Their upstream-pristine digests, measured before the first edit,
# are recorded in UPSTREAM.md so the anchor survives:
#
#     build.zig       extended in place by the fork's build definition
#     build.zig.zon   extended in place: .version, .fingerprint, .paths
#     .gitignore      upstream's 44 lines kept, fork ignore rules appended
#     README.md       replaced in place by the fork's README; upstream's exact
#                     bytes are carried whole at README.upstream.md, which is
#                     the path the record below names, with the same digest
#
# Also absent, by role rather than by origin -- every one of these is a
# fork-authored file, and the only licence asserted over any of them is the MIT
# grant in FORK-LICENSE.md, which covers the fork's own files and nothing else:
#
#     UPSTREAM.md  UPSTREAM.sha256  NOTICE.md  README.zig.md  FORK-NOTES.md
#     CHANGELOG.md  README.md  FORK-LICENSE.md
#     package.nix  flake.nix  devenv.nix  devenv.yaml  .envrc
#     .github/workflows/verify.yml
#     cross-test.profile.sh  zig/**  tests.zig  smoke.zig  consumer/**
#
# `.zig-cache/`, `zig-out/` and `.git/` are build output and VCS metadata and are
# never recorded.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOW THE DIGESTS WERE PRODUCED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Read each file as raw bytes and hash with SHA-256 (hashlib.sha256 over the
# byte string, in one call, no encoding step) on 2026-10-03. Same method for
# every record. No shell hashing command and no git command produced these
# lines. A tree walk over the repository reported no symlinks and no
# non-regular entries, so each record is the digest of that file's own bytes
# and not of a link target.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CHECKING THIS IN AN UNPACKED PACKAGE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# This record is written for the working tree, and it is deliberately a
# superset of what a dependent receives: `build.zig.zon` `.paths` is what
# travels. In a fetched package the upstream paths outside `.paths` will be
# reported missing by `sha256sum -c`; that is expected, not a failure of the
# record. The paths that MUST be in `.paths` for the package to build and for
# its tests to embed their corpora are the native core (`utf8proc.h`,
# `utf8proc.c`, `utf8proc_data.c`), `LICENSE.md`, `README.upstream.md`, all six
# `testdata/` files, `build.zig` and `build.zig.zon`.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STATUS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# SOURCE-CONFIRMED / PENDING-VERIFICATION. These digests were measured, not
# validated by a gate. No `sha256sum -c UPSTREAM.sha256` run is claimed by this
# file. The driver runs that gate; until it does, the verification section of
# README.zig.md carries no observed result for it.
#
